-- gap[104] · the branch as the function's ANSWER, reported by EXIT CODE.
--
-- THE RULE THIS FIXTURE CARRIES: when a program produces no output, do not test
-- its control flow with output. Three diagnoses of this defect were withdrawn
-- because each probed the branch with `print` while `print` was the instrument
-- that was broken — the branch was taken the whole time. This row asks the
-- question without going through any emission at all: rc=7 means the true arm
-- ran, rc=3 means it did not.
--
-- It is also the negative control for the tail-slot machinery in the other
-- direction: here the `if` IS the function's tail, so it must still be allowed
-- to return rather than being lowered as a bare effect.

main = (): i64
    if 42 > 10
        return 7
    3
